ISOpropyl for Debian and Ubuntu
===============================

This is an upstream-built alpha package for amd64 and arm64. Its dependency set
has been checked against Debian 13 and Ubuntu 24.04/26.04 LTS. It is not yet an
official Debian or Ubuntu archive package, and installed VM certification is
still pending on both architectures.

The package installs ISOpropyl's unprivileged GUI and CLI together with the
fixed root-owned PolicyKit helper and all three exact action policies. Never run
the GUI or CLI with sudo; both entry points reject root execution. No
package-owned file is setuid, and there are no maintainer scripts that download
software, start services, or access block devices.

The official distro archives do not currently contain every exact version in
ISOpropyl's pinned Authenticode analysis backend. That analysis therefore
reports unavailable in this package instead of using relaxed pins or a
substitute trust implementation. The normal inspection, hashing, DBX advice,
download authentication, media construction, and write-verification paths do
not depend on that backend.

This package does not remove the alpha release gates documented in SECURITY.md:
installed PolicyKit/SCM_RIGHTS race testing, power-loss and hot-swap testing,
QEMU boot testing, and representative physical-media certification remain
required before production use. Test only with expendable media and keep full
verification enabled.
